From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:31:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ui/sdl2: hand guest display planes to weston subsurfaces
 (opt-in)

In the RPi4 AAOS "HMI + video" layout the guest display is not one
directly scanned-out buffer: a scaled primary plane (the WebView video
underlay, DomA kernel virtio_gpu.plane_scaling=1) sits under three
overlay planes. qemu blends these with V3D and swaps, and weston then
composites qemu's window with V3D again.

With /run/qemu-plane-handoff present (checked at most once a second; off
when absent), qemu no longer blends the planes. Each plane's guest
texture is exported as a dmabuf (BROADCOM_UIF) and attached to its own
wl_subsurface of the SDL window, the primary scaled with wp_viewport,
and weston composites them. A full-screen direct scanout of a video
buffer (isp-scanout / sand-scanout) takes precedence; when neither
applies the GL blend is used as before.

Measured on the RPi4 (same device model, flag off/on): local 720p60 in
the HMI layout 52.0/51.9 -> 56.7/57.5 fps, Chromium drops 8 -> 2%, V3D
render qemu+weston 37.5 -> 16.6% (TFU 14.5 -> 22%); a streamed video in
the HMI layout 32.6/32.9 -> 44.1/41.1 fps (DomA CPU is the limit there);
fullscreen 1080p60 (direct scanout) and Gallery unchanged; touch works.

The guest is not held back: the guest's next write to a buffer and
weston's read of it are V3D jobs on the same BO, ordered by v3d's
implicit sync (v3d_submit.c: every job waits on the BO's fences and adds
its done fence as WRITE). Holding the guest until weston's frame
callback or buffer release was tried and cost 20-24 ms per frame (42
fps).

Design points:

  - GL texture names are recycled, so the dmabuf cache is keyed by the
    virtio resource id as well as the texture name and size, and an
    entry is dropped when the guest unrefs its resource (a hook in
    virtio-gpu-virgl.c). Keying by name and size alone showed another
    resource's old buffer.
  - A plane that moves or resizes is first unmapped in its own parent
    commit, and every plane is clipped to the window: otherwise weston
    can apply the new position before the new size and end the client
    for a geometry past the fullscreen size (xdg_wm_base error 4).
  - The subsurfaces get an empty input region, so touch and pointer
    input stays with the SDL window.

Adds ui/viewporter-protocol.c and ui/viewporter-client-protocol.h,
generated with wayland-scanner from wayland-protocols
stable/viewporter/viewporter.xml.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [depends on this layer's direct-scanout and primary-rect patches; RPi4 HMI tuning]
